Overview
The Random Hadith Generator is a web-based application that displays random Islamic hadiths to users by fetching data from a local JSON file containing an array of hadiths.
Key Characteristics:

Local JSON data storage with random selection
Alternative RESTful API integration available
Real-time data fetching with loading states
CSS animations for smooth transitions

High-Level Architecture
mermaidgraph TD
    A[User Browser] --> B[index.html]
    B --> C[script.js]
    C --> D[ahadith.json]
    C -.-> E[Vercel API - Alternative]
    E -.-> F[Hadith Database]
The system uses a client-side architecture where JavaScript fetches hadith data from a local JSON file. An alternative external API integration (Vercel) is available but not currently active.
Core Components

HTML Interface (index.html) - Basic page structure with hadith display area
JavaScript Controller (script.js) - Handles data fetching and DOM manipulation
Stylesheet (style.css) - Visual styling with animations and responsive design
Local Data Store (ahadith.json) - Contains array of hadith objects

Data Flow
When the user clicks "New Hadith":

JavaScript calls findrandomhadith()
Local ahadith.json file is fetched
Random hadith is selected from the array
Data is displayed on page with animation

Code Implementation
Primary Hadith Fetch Function (Local Data)
File: script.js
javascriptasync function findrandomhadith() {
  try {
    newHadithButton.innerText = 'Loading Hadith...';
    const response = await fetch('ahadith.json');
    const dataarray = await response.json();
    const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * dataarray.length);
    const data = dataarray[randomIndex];
    displayHadith(data.hadith_english, data.header, data.book);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error fetching Hadith:', error);
    newHadithButton.innerText = 'Failed to load Hadith';
  }
}
Explanation: This function fetches hadith data from a local JSON file, randomly selects one hadith from the array, and passes it to the display function. It provides user feedback by updating the button text during loading and on error.

Alternative API Function (External Data - Not Currently Used)
File: script.js
javascriptasync function fetchRandomHadith() {
  try {
    newHadithButton.innerText = 'Loading Hadith...';
    const response = await fetch('https://random-hadith-generator.vercel.app/bukhari/');
    const data = await response.json();
    console.log(data);
    displayHadith(data.data.hadith_english, data.data.header, data.data.book);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error fetching Hadith:', error);
    newHadithButton.innerText = 'Failed to load Hadith';
  }
}
Explanation: This alternative function fetches hadith data from the Vercel API. It is defined in the code but not currently attached to any event listener.
Display Function
File: script.js
javascriptfunction displayHadith(hadith, narrator, book) {
  // Reset animation
  hadithElement.style.animation = 'none';
  hadithElement.offsetHeight; // trigger reflow
  hadithElement.style.animation = '';

  hadithElement.innerText = hadith;
  narratorElement.innerText = narrator;
  bookElement.innerText = book;

  // Apply animation
  hadithElement.style.animation = 'fadeInUp 1s forwards';

  newHadithButton.innerText = 'New Hadith';
}
Explanation: Updates the page with the hadith content. Includes animation reset and reapplication for smooth transitions, and resets the button text after loading completes.

Event Listener
File: script.js
javascriptnewHadithButton.addEventListener('click', findrandomhadith);
Explanation: Attaches the findrandomhadith function to the "New Hadith" button click event.
Integration Points
Local Data Source (Currently Active): ahadith.json
Array of hadith objects with the following structure:
json[
  {
    "hadith_english": "...",
    "header": "...",
    "book": "..."
  }
]

External API (Available but not currently used): https://random-hadith-generator.vercel.app/bukhari/
Returns JSON format:
json{
  "data": {
    "hadith_english": "...",
    "header": "...",
    "book": "..."
  }
}

Font Services: Google Fonts CDN for typography
- Nunito Sans (hadith text)
- Multiple font families loaded for styling flexibility
Configuration
The application is configured to use local data by default:
- Data source: ahadith.json file in the root directory
- To switch to external API: Change line 49 in script.js from findrandomhadith to fetchRandomHadith

Data Structure Requirements:
The ahadith.json file should contain an array of hadith objects with these properties:
- hadith_english: The English translation of the hadith
- header: The narrator information
- book: The source book reference

Monitoring and Operations
Error Handling:
- Console logging for debugging: console.error('Error fetching Hadith:', error);
- User feedback via button text changes:
  - Loading state: "Loading Hadith..."
  - Error state: "Failed to load Hadith"
  - Default state: "New Hadith"

Visual Feedback:
- CSS fadeInUp animation (1s duration) applied to hadith text
- Button hover effects with color transitions
- Loading states provide real-time user feedback
